  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Peace Agreement&apos;s Transitional Justice System</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at contributing to the Comprehensive System of Truth, Justice, Reparation, and Non-Repetition (SIVJRNR Spanish acronym) implementation promoting victims&#x2019; participation. The project includes the following three components:Component 1: This component seeks to improve and strengthen the SIVJRNR entities&#x2019; technical and operational capacities to perform their duties and build peace within the provisions of Chapter 5 of the Peace Agreement by designing and delivering technical and operational tools.Component 2: This component seeks to promote the participation of victims, former FARC-EP combatants, and civil society organizations in the participation spaces of the SIVJRNR defined in the Peace Agreement, through strategies, tools, and actions to disseminate information that will allow the institutions to inform about their decision-making spaces and mechanisms, and the victims to understand and actively participate. Component 3: This component seeks to strengthen the capacities of the Government and Civil Society to design and develop actions aimed at increasing trust in the Peace Agreement implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
